# Sprint 14 — Second Enterprise Endpoint

## Objective

Deploy a second enterprise Windows workstation into the corp.lab Active Directory environment and integrate it into the existing SOC telemetry pipeline.

## System Deployed

| Hostname | Role | Domain |
|---|---|---|
| WIN11-02 | Corporate Workstation | corp.lab |

## Configuration

WIN11-02 was configured with:

- Windows 11
- VMware Tools
- Static IPv4 addressing
- Active Directory domain membership
- Corporate Group Policy
- Windows Security auditing
- PowerShell operational logging
- Sysmon endpoint telemetry
- Splunk Universal Forwarder

## Active Directory Integration

WIN11-02 was joined to corp.lab and moved into the existing workstation organizational unit to inherit the same security policies as WIN11-01.

Domain authentication, DNS resolution, Group Policy processing, and domain controller discovery were validated.

## Endpoint Telemetry

The endpoint provides multiple telemetry sources to the SOC:

- Windows Security Event Log
- Sysmon Operational Log
- PowerShell Operational Log

## SIEM Integration

Splunk Universal Forwarder was installed and configured to send endpoint telemetry to SIEM01.

Forwarder configuration was validated using Splunk btool before service restart.

## Validation

The following were confirmed in Splunk:

- WIN11-02 appeared as an active monitored host.
- Windows Security events were searchable.
- Sysmon process telemetry was searchable.
- PowerShell telemetry was searchable.
- Successful authentication events were visible.
- Failed authentication events were visible.
- Existing detections were capable of monitoring the new endpoint.

## SOC Architecture Improvement

The lab now contains multiple enterprise endpoints monitored by a centralized SIEM.

This allows future attack scenarios to distinguish between normal activity, compromised systems, and cross-host behavior.

## Outcome

WIN11-02 was successfully deployed as the second fully monitored corporate endpoint in the Enterprise SOC environment.
